THE FEATURE
Two optional params.csv settings control which CSV values DMS wrote become SQL NULL,
applied IDENTICALLY in the full load, CDC and validation (so validation can't false-flag
a correctly-loaded row):
  - null_values (all columns): '|'-separated exact strings -> NULL. Blank = today
    (the endpoint CsvNullValue, resolved by resolve_task, passed as --csv_null_value).
    Set, it REPLACES that marker list for every column.
  - null_rules (per-column): 'schema.table.column=none|V1|V2' entries joined by ';'.
    'none' keeps the text 'NULL' as data; a list replaces the default for that column.
    Names match case-insensitively; values match exactly/case-sensitively.
  - Precedence: rule > values > endpoint marker. Empty fields are ALWAYS NULL (unchanged).
  - Both blank/absent => BYTE-IDENTICAL to today (proven by a test).

